WEBVTT

00:00:00.598 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.708 --> 00:00:04.830
In this lesson, we cut a classic short men's style:

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:10.590
short on the sides and back, blending softly into a longer top, with a neat outline.

00:00:11.126 --> 00:00:13.630
You heard the reason for each step in the theory lesson.

00:00:13.943 --> 00:00:14.990
Here, we do it.

00:00:15.645 --> 00:00:16.362
Step one:

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:17.402
preparation.

00:00:18.081 --> 00:00:19.082
Wash your hands.

00:00:19.345 --> 00:00:20.389
Clippers, guards,

00:00:20.339 --> 00:00:25.242
combs and scissors have all been cleaned and disinfected after the previous client.

00:00:25.852 --> 00:00:28.896
Wrap a disposable neck strip around the client's neck,

00:00:28.846 --> 00:00:31.002
and only then fasten the cape over it.

00:00:31.687 --> 00:00:32.461
Step two:

00:00:32.736 --> 00:00:36.141
the consultation, as in the consultation and sectioning lesson.

00:00:36.726 --> 00:00:40.856
Ask how short the client wants the sides, how much to leave on top,

00:00:40.806 --> 00:00:42.621
a square or rounded neckline,

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:44.461
and where the sideburns should end.

00:00:44.941 --> 00:00:47.501
Agree using the guard, or with your fingers:

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:50.301
this guard on the sides, this much on top.

00:00:50.728 --> 00:00:54.701
Also ask how the last cut was done, and whether there was anything they didn't like.

00:00:54.946 --> 00:00:58.381
What the client doesn't like often matters more than what they do like.

00:00:58.811 --> 00:01:02.861
Comb the hair in a few directions, look for whorls, and check the scalp.

00:01:03.454 --> 00:01:04.232
Step three:

00:01:04.493 --> 00:01:05.432
dampen the hair.

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:10.552
Mist evenly, combing as you spray, in the direction the hair falls naturally.

00:01:10.883 --> 00:01:12.632
Evenly damp, not dripping.

00:01:13.216 --> 00:01:16.248
Many barbers do the clipper work on clean, dry hair,

00:01:16.198 --> 00:01:18.312
then dampen it for the scissor work.

00:01:18.648 --> 00:01:22.515
Either way is fine, as long as the hair is clean, combed straight,

00:01:22.465 --> 00:01:23.672
and free of tangles.

00:01:24.252 --> 00:01:25.112
Step four:

00:01:25.292 --> 00:01:27.832
the sides and back, with a guarded clipper.

00:01:28.419 --> 00:01:31.352
Start with the agreed guard, or a slightly longer one.

00:01:31.861 --> 00:01:34.792
Place the guard flat against the head, at the hairline.

00:01:35.221 --> 00:01:41.124
Move upward, against the growth, slowly and steadily, and around the parietal ridge,

00:01:41.074 --> 00:01:41.752
ease off,

00:01:41.862 --> 00:01:43.192
and flick the wrist outward.

00:01:43.756 --> 00:01:45.432
Overlap each pass a little.

00:01:45.903 --> 00:01:50.472
Near the ear, fold the ear down gently with a finger, to keep it out of the way.

00:01:50.711 --> 00:01:51.992
The back is the same:

00:01:52.181 --> 00:01:54.552
work from the nape up to the occipital bone.

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:55.832
Don't press hard.

00:01:56.261 --> 00:02:00.623
After that pass, comb the hair down, and go over it again in another direction,

00:02:00.573 --> 00:02:02.152
so you don't miss any hairs.

00:02:02.824 --> 00:02:07.698
If the client wants the very bottom even shorter, and you agreed on it beforehand,

00:02:07.648 --> 00:02:08.874
use a shorter guard,

00:02:08.985 --> 00:02:11.514
or no guard, only along the bottom edge.

00:02:12.019 --> 00:02:14.634
If you have not agreed on it, don't do it on your own.

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:17.434
Once it is short, you can't make it long again.

00:02:18.103 --> 00:02:18.962
Step five:

00:02:19.206 --> 00:02:22.002
scissor over comb, blending the sides upward.

00:02:22.479 --> 00:02:25.606
Place the comb close to the head where the clipper stopped,

00:02:25.556 --> 00:02:26.962
teeth angled slightly out.

00:02:27.301 --> 00:02:29.349
Cut the hair that sticks through the comb,

00:02:29.299 --> 00:02:31.442
with the blade running parallel to the comb.

00:02:31.959 --> 00:02:35.446
Move the comb gradually up, angling it out more and more,

00:02:35.396 --> 00:02:38.402
so the hair gets gradually longer toward the top.

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:41.122
Go all around the sides, then the back.

00:02:41.295 --> 00:02:43.122
Never stay long in one spot.

00:02:43.766 --> 00:02:44.646
Step six:

00:02:44.755 --> 00:02:45.366
the top.

00:02:45.675 --> 00:02:49.206
Section off the top, from the corners of the forehead back to the crown.

00:02:49.619 --> 00:02:52.524
Take a thin section at the front, lift it straight up,

00:02:52.474 --> 00:02:56.806
at a right angle to the scalp, and hold it between your index and middle fingers.

00:02:57.138 --> 00:02:58.406
Cut to the agreed length.

00:02:58.568 --> 00:02:59.606
This is your guideline.

00:02:59.955 --> 00:03:01.787
Then take the next section behind it,

00:03:01.737 --> 00:03:04.726
including a little hair from the previous section, to follow.

00:03:04.893 --> 00:03:09.206
Carry on like this, from the front back to the crown, keeping the same elevation.

00:03:09.612 --> 00:03:13.718
At the whorl on the crown, leave it a little longer, and use light tension,

00:03:13.668 --> 00:03:15.286
so the hair doesn't stand up.

00:03:15.622 --> 00:03:19.126
Stop now and then, look in the mirror, and ask the client:

00:03:19.476 --> 00:03:20.646
is this length okay?

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:23.844
After cutting in one direction, cross-check.

00:03:24.352 --> 00:03:28.217
Comb the hair up in horizontal sections, from one side to the other,

00:03:28.167 --> 00:03:29.844
hold it between your fingers,

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:31.524
and see whether the length is even.

00:03:32.022 --> 00:03:34.484
Any piece that sticks up, trim it to match.

00:03:35.111 --> 00:03:35.935
Step seven:

00:03:36.267 --> 00:03:38.095
connect the top with the sides.

00:03:38.522 --> 00:03:42.815
At the corner where the sides meet the top, there is often still a slight ridge.

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:47.259
Use scissor over comb, or cut that corner hair out toward the outside,

00:03:47.209 --> 00:03:49.695
until you can run your hand up from below,

00:03:49.804 --> 00:03:51.295
and no longer see a step.

00:03:51.716 --> 00:03:53.055
Look from the side to check.

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:54.433
Step eight:

00:03:54.615 --> 00:03:55.393
the outline.

00:03:55.808 --> 00:03:58.775
Around the ear, fold the ear down gently with a finger,

00:03:58.725 --> 00:04:02.593
and use the trimmer to create a natural curve that follows the hairline.

00:04:02.941 --> 00:04:03.953
Don't cut too high.

00:04:04.283 --> 00:04:05.233
The sideburns:

00:04:05.501 --> 00:04:07.233
cut them the same on both sides.

00:04:07.493 --> 00:04:11.473
Have the client sit up straight, head straight, looking straight into the mirror.

00:04:11.742 --> 00:04:14.433
Place a finger at the bottom of each sideburn to compare.

00:04:14.924 --> 00:04:15.633
The neckline:

00:04:15.738 --> 00:04:18.433
square or rounded, exactly as agreed.

00:04:18.832 --> 00:04:22.165
Have the client tip their head down slightly, tidy the edge,

00:04:22.115 --> 00:04:24.353
and don't push the neckline up too high.

00:04:25.039 --> 00:04:25.894
Step nine:

00:04:26.062 --> 00:04:26.854
the finish.

00:04:27.188 --> 00:04:30.614
Brush the loose hair off the neck and around the ears with a neck brush.

00:04:30.962 --> 00:04:33.494
Remove the cape, and throw away the neck strip.

00:04:33.877 --> 00:04:37.642
Work in a little styling product, the way the client will style it at home,

00:04:37.592 --> 00:04:38.534
and show them how.

00:04:38.919 --> 00:04:41.287
Finally, hold a hand mirror behind them,

00:04:41.237 --> 00:04:43.894
so the client can see the nape and the sides.

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:46.054
Ask whether they would like anything adjusted.

00:04:46.292 --> 00:04:49.414
If they do, adjust it right then, cheerfully.

00:04:49.785 --> 00:04:53.174
Don't let the client get home, and only then find they are unhappy.

00:04:53.791 --> 00:04:56.553
Before the client leaves, write it in the client record:

00:04:56.947 --> 00:05:01.593
which guard on the sides, how long on top, square or rounded neckline.

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:04.313
Next time, the client only has to say:

00:05:04.419 --> 00:05:05.513
same as last time.

00:05:05.942 --> 00:05:08.953
And book the next appointment, usually in three to five weeks.

00:05:09.581 --> 00:05:10.951
After the client leaves:

00:05:11.091 --> 00:05:15.323
brush the hair out of the clipper blade, disinfect the blade, guards,

00:05:15.273 --> 00:05:17.991
combs and scissors as the product instructs,

00:05:18.257 --> 00:05:21.271
oil the blade, and sweep up the hair under the chair.

00:05:21.609 --> 00:05:24.551
And now, please take the short quiz below the video.
